# Spec 024 — Maintenance model, running costs, brand filter, selection tray, recommendations

Status: Draft
Owner: <you>
Related: 022-car-tco (engine, market model, API, core screens), 023-market-checklist
(Market map, Checklist). Source: user feedback collected by the owner on
2026-11-02 and the owner's second used-listings export.

## Overview

Four pieces of user feedback and one data delivery:

1. "Some of the data sets (maintenance) seemed low." They are: service is one
   placeholder per year for every car, there is no age or km dependence, and
   wear, repairs, inspection, wheel changes and tolls are missing entirely.
2. "The Market plot should filter by brand."
3. "The model list on Your situation will get out of hand as models are added."
4. "The tool should give recommendations from the data."
5. The owner's second export adds twelve variants (Leaf, XC40, EV6, ID.3,
   Model Y RWD, e-208, Corsa-e, Zoe, 500e, Dolphin).

Order of delivery is 5 → 1 → 2 → 3 → 4: the data first, then the numbers
people already see, then the two small UI changes, then recommendations,
which benefit from the larger catalogue and the corrected costs.

## Context

- Engine line items today (`engine/schedule.py`): purchase, fees,
  re-registration, lease/loan payments, insurance, traffic tax, energy, tyres
  (winter set at purchase + replacement by km), service (annual amount spread
  monthly), delay, and the exit terms. Everything is integer øre, provenance
  per input, and every default is an estimate with a basis.
- Published Norwegian sources found on 2026-11-02 (URLs in
  `docs/cars/sources.md`): OFV "Kostnader ved bilhold 2026" (new car, three
  years, no age split; EV service and repairs 3 366–5 786 kr/yr by price
  class, tyres at 37 000 km life including two wheel changes a year);
  Kia's published EV service prices (7 990 kr every 2 yr/30 000 km for the
  EV6; 1 990/3 690 kr for cars 7+ years); Bertel O. Steen's Stellantis EV
  prices (first service 2 490 kr at 1 yr/12 500 km, then 4 290 kr every
  2 yr/25 000 km, brake fluid 1 490 kr every 2 yr); Smarte Penger's repair
  cost per km by odometer (0.11 kr/km at 20 000 km rising to 0.96 kr/km at
  110 000+ km, not EV-specific); Statens vegvesen's inspection cycle (first
  within four years of first registration, then every two years) with
  station prices 1 070–1 619 kr; city toll rates for electric cars effective
  2026 (Oslo 21/26 kr, Bergen 17.60/35.20 kr, Trondheim 12.32/24.64 kr,
  Nord-Jæren 16.80 kr) with hourly and monthly caps; Skatteetaten's 2026
  traffic-insurance tax for EVs (9.16 kr/day from 1 Mar 2026; 8.96 from
  1 Mar 2025; 9.41 proposed for 2027) and the 2026 re-registration table
  (7 505 / 4 532 / 1 942 kr by first-registration year band, over 1 200 kg).
- Brand warranties and service intervals as sold in Norway were confirmed
  for every catalogue make (Tesla 5 yr/100 000 km, no fixed service
  interval; Hyundai 5 yr unlimited, 2 yr/30 000 km; Kia 7 yr/150 000 km,
  2 yr/30 000 km; VW and Skoda 5 yr/100 000 km, every 2 yr; Nissan
  5 yr/100 000 km, 1 yr/30 000 km; Volvo 5 yr/150 000 km, 2 yr/30 000 km;
  Peugeot/Opel/Fiat 5 yr/100 000 km; MG 7 yr/150 000 km, 1 yr/24 000 km;
  BYD 6 yr/150 000 km, 2 yr/30 000 km). Where a brand publishes no price
  the seed carries an estimate with the comparable published price as basis.

## Requirements

### Data

- **R0 — Second vehicle batch.** The owner's `target_variant` export shape
  converts alongside the first shape; twelve variants join the catalogue
  with importer warranties; the bundle is refitted and the backtest report
  regenerated. Delivered in commit `024 R0`.

### Maintenance and running costs (engine)

- **R1 — Scheduled service by interval.** `VehicleInputs` gains a service
  block: `service_interval_months`, `service_interval_km`,
  `service_price_ore` (per service), optional `service_first_price_ore`
  (a cheaper first service, as Stellantis prices it) and optional
  `service_price_after_7y_ore` (Kia's published older-car price). The engine
  books a service in the month either interval elapses since the previous
  one, counting from month 0 (a sold car is assumed serviced at sale; for a
  private used purchase the next service is due at the interval from
  purchase and the item is an estimate). A lease that includes service
  zeroes it, as today. Brands with no fixed interval (Tesla) carry
  `service_interval_months: 0` and are costed through R2 only.
- **R2 — Wear and repairs allowance.** New cash item `wear_and_repairs`:
  (a) a per-year wear amount per variant (`wear_per_year_ore`: wipers,
  cabin filter, brake fluid and a 12 V battery amortised over their
  published intervals, seeded from the parts prices found), and (b) a
  repair allowance per km that rises with the odometer, from a rates table
  (`repair_kr_per_km_by_odometer` bands, `repair_ev_factor`,
  `repair_in_warranty_factor`). The in-warranty factor applies while the
  vehicle warranty (years and km) still runs. Every value is an estimate
  with the source and basis in `rates.yaml`.
- **R3 — Periodic inspection.** New cash item `inspection`: the rule
  `periodic_inspection` in `rules/tax_rules.yaml` (first inspection within
  48 months of first registration, then every 24 months, source Statens
  vegvesen) and `inspection_fee_nok` in `rates.yaml` (estimate with the
  station price range as its band). The engine books the fee in the month
  the next inspection falls due, using the model year's mid-year as the
  first-registration month when the listing has none.
- **R4 — Tyres and wheel changes.** Tyre life default becomes 37 000 km
  (OFV), and `wheel_change_nok` (two changes a year, estimate from the
  NAF/BOS prices) is added to the `tyres` item each year. Dekkhotell
  storage is not modelled (optional and local).
- **R5 — Tolls.** New profile field `toll_passages_per_week` (default 0)
  and a `tolls` seed (`data/cars/seed/tolls.yaml`): per-municipality EV
  rate per passage off-peak and rush, the hour rule, the monthly cap and
  the source URL. New cash item `tolls` = passages × 52/12 × a 50/50
  off-peak/rush blend, capped by the monthly cap, zero when the
  municipality has no toll ring on file or passages are 0. The Situation
  screen gains the field next to municipality with the hint "trips through
  the toll ring per week, both directions count".
- **R6 — Tax rule corrections.** Traffic-insurance tax for EVs: 8.96 kr/day
  from 2025-03-01, 9.16 from 2026-03-01 (`live`, checked 2026-11-02), 9.41
  from 2027-03-01 as `pending` (proposal). Re-registration 2026 bands:
  7 505 / 4 532 / 1 942 kr (`live`, checked 2026-11-02); 2025 values stay
  `unverified`. Rules remain the only place these numbers live.
- **R7 — Display and provenance.** The Compare and Detail screens show a
  "Service and repairs" display row (service + wear and repairs +
  inspection) and a "Tolls" row; line items stay separate on Detail with
  their inputs, sources, status and bases. Input labels for every new input
  id are added to `INPUT_LABELS`.
- **R8 — Golden cases.** The six existing golden cases keep their expected
  values (their fixtures set the new items to zero explicitly). A new golden
  case `g7_maintenance` with a worked example in `docs/cars/golden/`
  exercises service events, the first-service price, the warranty
  boundary of the repair allowance, inspections at 48 and 72 months of age
  and wheel changes. Property tests: cumulative service and inspection
  schedules are non-decreasing; a car with more km never has a lower
  repair allowance; leases that include service have zero service.

### Market and selection (frontend)

- **R9 — Brand filter.** The Market filter rail gains a "Brand" select built
  from the catalogue, wired to the existing `make` query parameter of both
  market endpoints; the text search keeps matching model and trim.
- **R10 — Selection tray on Situation.** The per-variant checkbox list is
  replaced by a compact "Your selection" tray: one chip per selected variant
  with its year range (editable) and a remove button, an "Add a car"
  search-as-you-type box over the catalogue grouped by make (keyboard
  navigable, 44 px targets), and the "Browse the market" link. Compare's
  "Edit selection" affordance points to `/cars/market`. Behaviour of
  `selection` in state and URL is unchanged.

### Recommendations

- **R11 — Recommend endpoint.** `POST /api/cars/recommend` takes the same
  profile as `/scenarios` (no selection), builds every option the catalogue
  and the user's limits allow (all variants × model years × allowed modes,
  with the `both` pay mode expanded as today), ranks by the requested
  measure and returns the top `n` (default 5, max 10) as `OptionSummary`
  rows plus per-row reasons: lowest expected cost, narrowest P10–P90 band,
  best fun score within budget, lowest cash up front. Rate limit
  `CARS_SCENARIO_LIMIT`; memoised like scenarios; draws capped at 1 000 for
  this endpoint to stay inside the two-second budget with the full
  catalogue. Response carries `n_considered`, `ruled_out` counts by reason,
  and the status/material-estimate labels of each row.
- **R12 — Recommendations UI.** A "Start here" card on Situation (shown once
  the profile validates) with the top three and a button to put them in the
  selection, and a "Recommended for you" strip on Compare with the same
  rows and a link to put any of them in the selection. Every row shows the
  Live/Estimate badge and its material-estimate labels, so a car ranked on
  placeholder prices is visibly flagged.

### Cross-cutting

- **R13 — Tests.** Backend: service event schedule, first-service price,
  repair allowance bands and warranty boundary, inspection cycle, tolls with
  cap, tax-rule lookup for the corrected dates, recommend endpoint shape and
  limits, runtime-import guard still passes. Frontend: brand filter narrows
  dots and sends `make`; tray add/remove/years and typeahead keyboard flow;
  recommendations card renders from the mock fixture and adds to selection.
- **R14 — Docs.** `docs/cars/sources.md` gets the maintenance, inspection,
  toll and tax sources with URLs and dates; `decisions.md` records the
  modelling choices (repair curve scaling, Tesla as wear-only, blend for
  tolls); README and CLAUDE.md mention spec 024.

### Detail screen follow-up (user feedback 2026-11-03)

- **R15 — One exit point on Detail.** Detail carries the same "Mark an exit
  point" slider as Compare curves and both read one shared, session-only
  value (default 2.5 years). The first tile, the chart marker, the buying
  and selling strip and "Where the money goes" are all computed on the
  central path at that month, so they agree with each other to the krone;
  the simulated P10–P90 range sits beside the tile. The API returns
  `display_series` (every display row at months 0..60), `purchase_price`
  and `resale_band` (P10/P50/P90 of the sale value by month) so the screen
  needs no new request when the slider moves.
- **R16 — Purchase and sale assumptions.** A "Buying and selling" strip
  shows the purchase price with its source and status, the expected sale
  price at the marked exit with its likely range, and the value lost (price
  minus sale price plus the cost to sell). Leases show rent, rent paid to
  the exit and the cost to hand the car back instead.
- **R17 — Inputs table fits the page.** The table uses a fixed layout with
  wrapping cells (no sideways overflow on desktop), source URLs become
  links, and values are shown in display units (`display_value`, `unit`,
  `display_range` from the API: kroner not øre, per-year / per-km units,
  tax rules per energy type). Overrides typed in kroner are converted back
  to øre before they are sent.

## Out of Scope (explicit)

- Dekkhotell, parking fees, ferry fares, car washing: local and optional.
- Automated price lists and lease portals, the weekly ingest workflow and
  the quarantine review UI (spec 025).
- Norwegian UI.

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] R0: the live `/api/cars/vehicles` lists 22 variants and the Market map
      shows the new cohorts.
- [ ] R1–R4: on Detail for a used 2019 Leaf at 15 000 km/yr the Service and
      repairs row is a multiple of the old 3 000 kr/yr figure, every input
      in it carries a source and a basis, and the g7 worked example matches
      the engine to the øre.
- [ ] R5: entering Oslo and 10 passages a week adds a Tolls row that matches
      10 × 52/12 × the blended 2026 rate, capped at 120 passages a month.
- [ ] R6: `/api/cars/sources` lists no unverified traffic-tax rule for 2026.
- [ ] R9/R10: filtering the Market map to one brand sends `make=` and the
      Situation tray shows only the selected cars with working year edits.
- [ ] R11/R12: with the default profile, "Start here" returns three cars in
      under two seconds and pressing the button puts them in the selection.
- [ ] R13: `pytest`, `npm run test` and the Docker smoke pass in CI.
- [ ] R15–R17: on Detail, moving the exit slider changes the first tile,
      the chart marker, the sale price and the breakdown together; with the
      measure set to total cost the tile equals the breakdown total; the
      inputs table shows "131 308 kr", not "13130779", and needs no
      horizontal scroll at 1180 px.

